course: dictionary
lesson: 13013
title: A word from outer space
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Extraterrestrial is a long word, but it has parts you can spot. Extra means outside, and terrestrial means of the Earth. Put them together and extraterrestrial means coming from outside the Earth, in space. «The meteorite was an extraterrestrial rock that fell in the desert.» The rock did not start on Earth. It came from space.
explain: The word can also name a living being. An extraterrestrial is a being from another planet, which is often called an alien. «Many films show an extraterrestrial visiting Earth.» Here the word is a noun, a thing that is a being.
explain: Scientists use this word when they search for life beyond Earth. «Scientists are searching for extraterrestrial life on Mars.» They have looked for tiny living things called microbes, but none has been found yet. Aliens in films are imagined. No one has proved that they exist.
fact: Extraterrestrial is an adjective, and an extraterrestrial is a noun.
fact: Extra means outside, and terrestrial means of the Earth.
fact: «Meteorites» that land on Earth are extraterrestrial rocks, because they come from space.
fact: «E.T. the Extra-Terrestrial» is a famous film about an extraterrestrial who visits Earth.
fact: Scientists are still searching for extraterrestrial life, but no one has yet proved that any exists.
exercise: «The meteorite was an extraterrestrial rock that fell in the desert.» What does extraterrestrial mean here? | *Coming from outside the Earth | Made of pure gold | Found deep under the sea | Very hot inside the Earth
exercise: Ella says ET is a short name for a living being from another planet. Which word is it? | planet | *alien | scientist | rock
exercise: «Scientists are searching for extraterrestrial life on Mars.» Has any extraterrestrial life been found yet? | Yes, one was seen in a film | Yes, lots of microbes were found | *No, none has been found yet | Yes, on the Moon
test: «The film is about an extraterrestrial who visits Earth.» What does extraterrestrial mean in this sentence? | *From outside the Earth | Small and friendly | Shiny and made of metal | Found in a cave
test: Which statement is true about aliens in stories and films? | They only come to Earth at night | They live in every city on Earth | They are real and have been met by scientists | *They are imagined, and no one has proved they exist
exam: «Scientists found an extraterrestrial rock.» What does extraterrestrial mean? | Very small and light | Made of wood | Buried under the ground | *Coming from outside the Earth, in space
